[
  // ── CROSS-PROFESSION AND GLOBAL BONUSES ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  //
  // The Melvor layer GDD §4.1 has carried as "Planned": progress in one place paying off in
  // another. Every one of these pays into the SAME six quantities the mastery ladder does
  // (ProfessionBenefitKind), through the SAME ProfessionBenefits seam — which is why adding them
  // needed no change at all to ActionResolver or ProfessionSystem.
  //
  // ── THE AUTHORING RULE ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  //
  // A synergy must follow a chain the professions ALREADY have (docs/professions.md §5). Mining
  // pays Smithing because ore actually walks from one to the other; a synergy between two
  // professions that never touch would be a number pretending to be a relationship, and the
  // player would learn to read the table instead of the game.
  //
  // Source and target must differ — the validator refuses a profession paying for its own level,
  // because that is a mastery rung with extra steps, and a self-amplifying one.
  //
  // ── THE GLOBAL ROWS ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  //
  // A row with no "source" reads the player's TOTAL profession level (20 × 99 = 1980 at the
  // ceiling). That is what makes a global bonus something earned across the whole roster rather
  // than a constant hidden in a tuning class. They unlock late and pay little per level on
  // purpose: a global bonus is the reward for breadth, and breadth should not out-earn the
  // mastery of the action actually being performed.
  //
  // ── WHY THE CAPS ARE NOT ROUND ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  //
  // Same rule the mastery ladder follows: each "max" is exactly what its rate reaches at the
  // source's ceiling, because the validator refuses a cap the source can never deliver. A
  // promise the table can never keep is worse than a smaller honest one.
  //
  // ── STILL UNBALANCED ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  //
  // Every number here is a placeholder, like every other profession number in the game. Nobody
  // has played to level 99 of anything.

